<title>SINGAPORE: Teck Wah 1996 net plunges 98 pct.</title>
<headline>Teck Wah 1996 net plunges 98 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     0.05  vs   2.01</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		   4.00  vs   8.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    0.04  vs   1.86</p>
<p>    Turnover				51.05  vs  55.80</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.04  vs   0.02</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   0.98  vs   0.56</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     4.82  vs   4.10</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.13  vs   nil</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 1.52  vs   3.60</p>
<p>    Tax					1.16  vs   1.50</p>
<p>Note - Teck Wah Paper Products Ltd said its performance was affected by weak demand, a drop in selling prices, continued losses at its Chinese operations and start-up costs at its new Indonesian unit. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
